  partName: Back Cap
  description: The Back Cap is a compact, tiny component located at the middle-center-front
    of the jet engine, made from Shaft1 material. It plays a crucial role in sealing
    the engine's rear section, preventing gas leaks and maintaining optimal pressure.
    Interestingly, its small size belies its importance in ensuring the engine's
    overall efficiency and performance.
